<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Union of the Crowns</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1603">1603</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Union of the Crowns was the accession of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-vi-and-i">James VI of Scotland</a> to the thrones of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> and Ireland on the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elizabeth-i">Elizabeth I</a> in March 1603. The kingdoms kept their own parliaments, laws and churches but shared one monarch, who now lived in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> and governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> through the Privy Council in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edinburgh">Edinburgh</a>. The personal union lasted until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acts-of-union-1707">Acts of Union</a> of 1707.</p></div>
